				)
			)
		)
	)
	(text
		"NOTES\n1  U2 VIO (pin 5) to +5V and STBY (pin 8) to SGND are both\n   mandatory. Left off, the transceiver sits in standby and\n   sends nothing while every other measurement looks correct.\n2  C7 is 10 uF low-ESR on VDDCORE/VCAP (U1 pin 6) and is not\n   optional - the core regulator is unstable without it.\n   Pin 6 is not a port pin and must NEVER go to +5V. Keep the\n   PCB track to C7 under 6 mm. DS39977C 2.4 and table 31-4.\n3  R5 = 120R, DO NOT FIT. The car's bus is already terminated\n   at both ends and a third resistor overloads it. Footprint\n   and a \"120R DNF\" silkscreen legend only.\n4  C1 = C2 = 33 pF C0G, not 22 pF. Y1 is CL = 20 pF (crystal\n   datasheet: 20 pF std), and C = 2 x (CL - Cstray) with\n   Cstray about 5 pF gives 30 pF, so 33 pF from the E12 row."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 247.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bc9d8e5-f290-584d-a6c2-eac8fd1c4e23")
	)
	(text
		"\n5  J1 and J2 are wired in parallel on the same four nets, so\n   the cables are interchangeable and the board passes CAN\n   through even with U1 out of its socket. Micro-Fit pin\n   1 = +5V, 2 = SGND, 3 = CANH, 4 = CANL, fixed by the harness.\n6  Decoupling: C3 at U1 pin 20, C4 at U2 pin 3, C5 at U2 pin 5.\n7  No pull-ups, series diodes or capacitors on PGC/PGD - they\n   interfere with the programmer. DS39977C 2.5.\n8  J4 brings out every unused I/O pin plus power so a design\n   error can be patched with a wire. CANTX2/CANRX2 are the\n   ECAN alternates on RC6/RC7.\n9  Connections on this sheet are made by net label, not wire."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 247.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a22d417f-d46e-5c84-800a-8f2e3d67ab2d")
	)
